\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S4}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Actual TCP paths with different paired success outcomes} (r4e1 $C-F$). Examples are selected near the TCP-area median within each post-hoc success-change group, pooling all 240 r4e1 $C-F$ units of both tasks; all three selected cases are move\_near (seeds 1110, 1055, 1097). In groups of even size the two middle units tie, and floating-point rounding decided the pick. Paths are measured in the simulator world frame, with starts marked by dots and ends by stars. Axes differ across cases. Both arms execute the perturbation; C restores reference context, so later actions can differ. The cases are conditioned on the outcome and are not representative samples or causal subgroups. RGB observations were not stored.}}{10}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
